Edition No. 43 — Friday, 13 November 2026

10 stories: 'Zambia does not belong to an individual': the ten candidates Hichilema beat in August sign one statement against removing presidential term limits (lead); The maize money starts today: Moyo says farmers owed for 2025/26 deliveries to the FRA will be paid from Friday 13 November, drawing on K14.7 billion of the supplementary budget; From an operating loss to K6.3 billion after tax: Kapala hails ZESCO's turnaround on his first visit as Electricity Minister, and the utility's own report trims his K6.5 billion; 'No universal, one-size-fits-all' model: China's ambassador says Zambia's democracy should not be judged by a small number of outsiders, days after the EU's election dialogue; Forms Five and Six return: Kamboni sets February 2027 for Zambia's first A-level intake, open to Grade 12 leavers of 2024 to 2026, with university entry from 2029; A plea on 24 November and a ruling at 11:00 today: Mundubile and Zulu face the sedition charges without counsel, as the High Court rules on their account of the UN refuge; Bonds of K538,000 and two Toyotas: the ACC charges a Lusaka Archdiocese priest with concealing K1.5 million it links to a former Community Development officer's K5.6 million case; Fifty-six deaths and 2,658 suspected cases: cholera has added a thousand cases since late October, as the WHO offers help on water and the water minister calls in the NGOs; Free entry at Levy Mwanawasa and 'an element of madness': Zambia meet Burundi at 15:00 today with the President's tickets in the stands and four forwards missing; A 32-team knockout and a first women's national cup, backed by KCM's US$1.6 million; and in Philadelphia tonight, Patrick Chinyemba turns professional against an unbeaten American.


